        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I need to work out the intensive (yaṅ) formation of hṛṣ, which is ātmanepada, then apply the conditional ending for 2nd dual. For the intensive, the reduplication of a root with ṛ as upadhā follows the special rule turning the reduplicated syllable into \"rī\" per sutra 7.4.90.\n\nWorking through this, hṛṣ becomes jarīhṛṣya in the yaṅ, similar to varīvṛtya and narīnṛtya. Then applying the conditional with iṭ augment and the deletion of ya's vowel before an ārdhadhātuka ending (since yaṅ roots lose their final ya before consonant-initial suffixes), I arrive at ajarīhṛṣiṣyethām as the candidate 2nd dual conditional form.\n\nActually, sūtra 1.1.4 blocks guṇa when the ārdhadhātuka suffix causes lopa of a dhātu-part — here sya triggers yaṅ-lopa, so guṇa is blocked, giving jarīhṛṣiṣyate rather than a guṇated form. This parallels cases like varīvṛtitā from √vṛt yaṅ.\n\n",
